Lab 07: Windows 11 VM “My computer is so slow.” 

Goal: The lab plan

Part 1. Baseline: see what a healthy VM looks like in Task Manager.

Part 2. Break it: run a harmless loop that keeps the chef busy all the time.

Part 3. Troubleshoot: find the culprit in Task Manager, end it, then check Startup apps and Resource Monitor.

The analogy: a restaurant kitchen

CPU is the chef. It does the actual work. One chef can only cook so fast.

RAM is the bench space. It holds whatever the chef is working on right now. When the bench is full, things get stacked on the floor, and everything slows down.

Disk is the pantry. Fetching from there takes longer than grabbing something off the bench.

Network is the delivery door. Sometimes “slow” really means waiting on a delivery.

When someone says “it’s slow”, I need to work out what is overloaded.

